{% comment %}
  Resolves the canonical purchasable state of a product.

  Outputs one of: 'available' | 'coming_soon' | 'sold_out'

  Signal:
  - product.available == true                       -> 'available'  (normal buy)
  - product.available == false, no 'sold-out' tag   -> 'coming_soon' (pre-launch + waitlist)
  - product.available == false, has 'sold-out' tag  -> 'sold_out'    (discontinued, no waitlist)

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object (required)

  Usage (capture + strip, since snippets don't return values):
  {%- capture product_state -%}{%- render 'product-state', product: card_product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign product_state = product_state | strip -%}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign state = 'available'
  if product.available == false
    if product.tags contains 'sold-out'
      assign state = 'sold_out'
    else
      assign state = 'coming_soon'
    endif
  endif
  echo state
-%}
